            <ArticleTitle>Symptoms of rectosigmoid carcinoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1147-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The presenting symptoms of 167 patients with carcinoma of the rectum, sigmoid, and rectosigmoid were reviewed. The earliest symptom was a change in bowel habits and the most frequent symptom was visible blood in the stool followed by a change in bowel habits. The duration of symptoms was not related to survival or the stage of tumor found during surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
